ders rose 11% year on year, and cancellations were below 1%.\n- **Run-rate:** Quarterly revenue was C$905M in 2025Q3, C$960M in 2025Q4, C$980M in 2026Q1 and C$890M in 2026Q2 (n2.d3). Q2 was depressed by the plant outage. A normal quarter of about C$960–980M annualises to roughly C$3.9B. Reaching C$4.2B needs about C$1.05B a quarter, which is roughly 8% growth on the Q1 level.\n- **Outage:** The Halbrook plant builds all of Voltaris's large power transformers. It was offline for nine weeks in Q2 and restarted in August at full capacity (n2.d5, n2.d7). Delayed orders are to be delivered under a delivery recovery plan. This is a timing hit, not a loss of demand. Part of the Q2 shortfall, about C$80–90M, should shift into H2 2026 or 2027 and add to 2027 revenue.\n- **Weak point:** All large-transformer capacity sits at one site. Catching up on the delayed orders while serving new demand could be capacity-constrained. The backlog is only about 1.2 times guidance, so a slow recovery could leave 2027 short.\n\nMy estimate for 2027 revenue is about C$4.0–4.3B, with the guidance reachable but not comfortably so. I didn't find the delivery recovery plan itself, so I don't know its timeline. n3's industry-share view (n3.r1) leans below guidance, which is more cautious than my read.","ttft_ms":1620,"type":"result","duration_ms":50676,"uuid":"cb3b7535-391b-424b-b4a9-7e582f8a1b6a","ttft_stream_ms":916,"time_to_request_ms":70,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":4,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":9,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":3,"tool_pool_refresh":5,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":2,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":8,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":4,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":2,"request_build":6},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":20,"ti